--------------------- CableDyn Input File ------------------------------------
Floating Rigid6 buoy on three taut legs with a finite-EI cable clamped at its keel, swell
-- A surface-piercing 6-DOF buoy (80 t, 113 m^3 displaced, hydrostatic heave, roll, and pitch
-- restoring) in 100 m of water is held by three taut polyester legs at 120 deg. A finite-EI
-- dynamic cable leaves the keel point (Body1 point, 4 m below the waterline) and runs in -X to a
-- seabed anchor with a touchdown. END CONNECTIONS clamps the cable End A (Rigid) at 60 deg below
-- horizontal in the body frame; a pinned cable would hang off at about 82 deg. The direction
-- turns with the buoy and the clamp moment BendMom4N1 is returned to it, in the static solve
-- (bodyIC static) and in the dynamics. The first 10 m of cable use 0.25 m elements to resolve the
-- bending boundary layer at the clamp. Body1My is the net external pitch moment on the buoy
-- (zero at rest). 30 s of 1 m, 14 s Airy swell with an 8 s start-up ramp.
